        "original_id": "79620fd4-ba67-5ac9-96b7-cdb5827e1a19",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Collective for Living Cinema\n- People: Dziga Vertov, Jonathan Demme\n- Events: Made in Texas - New Films From Austin\n- Places: White Street, Lower Manhattan, New York City, Financial District, 8 Albany Street\n- Products: W New York - Downtown Hotel and Residences\n\nFacts:\n- Dziga Vertov, born David Abelevich Kaufman and also known as Denis Kaufman, was born on 2 January 1896 and died on 12 February 1954.\n- Dziga Vertov was a Soviet pioneer documentary film and newsreel director and a cinema theorist.\n- In October 1981, director Jonathan Demme presented the Made in Texas - New Films From Austin series at the Collective for Living Cinema in New York City.\n- The Collective for Living Cinema was an outpost of avant-garde cinema located on White Street in Lower Manhattan in the United States.\n- W New York - Downtown Hotel and Residences is a 630-foot building at 8 Albany Street in the Financial District of Lower Manhattan, New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
